body:
### Issue
Clang Static Analyzer `core.UndefinedBinaryOperatorResult` in `simulation_sysmem_manager.cpp:53`: `pcie_base_` is read before being written in `SimulationSysmemManager`.

### Description
`SysmemManager::pcie_base_` was declared without an initializer. `SiliconSysmemManager` sets it in its constructor, but `SimulationSysmemManager` never does — leaving it as a garbage value when used in `init_sysmem`:

```cpp
// simulation_sysmem_manager.cpp:53 — pcie_base_ was uninitialized
{system_memory_ + i * (1ULL << 30), channel_size, pcie_base_ + i * (1ULL << 30)}
```

Fix: initialize `pcie_base_ = 0` at the declaration site in the base class. Zero is the correct default for simulation (no real hardware), and `SiliconSysmemManager` still overrides it with the arch-specific value in its constructor.

Also removed a stale commented-out `const` variant of the same field.

### List of the changes
- `device/api/umd/device/chip_helpers/sysmem_manager.hpp`: initialize `pcie_base_ = 0`; remove stale `// const uint64_t pcie_base_;` comment

### Testing
Build-verified. No hardware required — the bug is in simulation-only code.

### API Changes
There are no API changes in this PR.

